WEBVTT

01:31.570 --> 01:33.230
<b>So how does that sound?</b>

01:33.570 --> 01:36.360
<b>I suppose I could help out 
<i>that</i> much, anyway.</b>

01:36.640 --> 01:38.190
<b>Excellent! Please do!</b>

01:40.220 --> 01:46.360
<b>2nd Stage: Lv. 2
A happy ending doesn't mean this game is over</b>

01:41.930 --> 01:43.480
<b>Do you really think that'll be</b>

01:43.480 --> 01:45.490
<b>enough to motivate Erika, though?</b>

01:45.490 --> 01:46.380
<b>Oh, don't worry.</b>

01:47.380 --> 01:49.370
<b>I've got other tricks up my sleeve.</b>

01:51.520 --> 01:52.880
<b>Aha...</b>

01:53.310 --> 01:55.430
<b>So that's what you had in mind?</b>

01:55.430 --> 01:57.210
<b>I <i>thought</i> something was afoot.</b>

01:57.860 --> 02:00.120
<b>Y'know, sometimes I'm surprised by</b>

02:00.120 --> 02:02.130
<b>how <i>nasty</i> you can be, Fumiya.</b>

02:02.130 --> 02:03.510
<b>Oh, shut up...</b>

02:03.750 --> 02:04.810
<b>But fine, I get it.</b>

02:05.470 --> 02:07.660
<b>I just need to let Erika 
know all casual-like, right?</b>

02:07.980 --> 02:09.340
<b>Right. Thanks.</b>

02:13.980 --> 02:16.530
<b><i>That's everything that needed to be done.</i></b>

02:17.100 --> 02:19.700
<b><i>All that's left is 
for the three arrows I've let fly</i></b>

02:20.440 --> 02:22.870
<b><i>to hit their mark according to plan.</i></b>

02:34.040 --> 02:35.550
<b>That's our Erika!</b>

02:35.550 --> 02:37.550
<b>Wow, a home run!</b>

02:39.320 --> 02:40.790
<b>Girls' Softball</b>

02:41.190 --> 02:42.800
<b><i>My strategy was a success.</i></b>

02:43.990 --> 02:46.830
<b><i>All three arrows scored critical hits.</i></b>

02:49.350 --> 02:51.430
<b><i>The final boss has been defeated.</i></b>

02:53.790 --> 02:56.310
<b>Yuzu Izumi: Conversation: A / Academics: C
Sports: B Friendship: A / Effort: B</b>

02:53.800 --> 02:55.370
<b>The first arrow was Izumi.</b>

02:56.340 --> 03:11.320
<b>Classroom / Konno's Motivation Meter / Day/Month</b>

02:56.610 --> 02:57.930
<b>Say, Erika...</b>

02:57.930 --> 03:01.310
<b>Now that I'm captain and all, 
could you help me out?</b>

03:01.310 --> 03:03.830
<b>We may as well make this fun for everyone.</b>

03:04.340 --> 03:08.400
<b><i>Konno apparently has 
a real soft spot for her friends,</i></b>

03:06.580 --> 03:11.340
<b>...</b>

03:08.400 --> 03:11.330
<b><i>and here's her pal Izumi 
asking her to pitch in.</i></b>

03:11.340 --> 03:14.340
<b>Aoi Hinami: Conversation: S / Academics: S
Sports: S / Friendship: A / Effort: S</b>

03:12.250 --> 03:14.340
<b><i>Next, the second arrow: Hinami.</i></b>

03:14.340 --> 03:36.360
<b>Gym / Konno's Motivation Meter / Day/Month</b>

03:15.010 --> 03:16.550
<b>Got a second, Mika?</b>

03:16.550 --> 03:17.670
<b>What is it?</b>

03:18.270 --> 03:20.470
<b>Erika's going to be in the game, right?</b>

03:20.470 --> 03:22.800
<b>Usually everyone participates.</b>

03:22.800 --> 03:24.350
<b>Good question. Beats me.</b>

03:24.780 --> 03:28.410
<b>Erika doesn't look like 
the softball type, after all.</b>

03:28.700 --> 03:32.360
<b>If she's not up to it, tell her she 
can get by with, like, one pinch-hit.</b>

03:32.360 --> 03:34.670
<b>Then you can leave everything else up to me!</b>

03:36.610 --> 03:41.870
<b>Gym / Konno's Motivation Meter / Day/Month</b>

03:37.740 --> 03:38.740
<b>Erika!</b>

03:37.800 --> 03:38.840
<b>Erika!</b>

03:38.740 --> 03:39.740
<b>Blah, blah, yadda yadda</b>

03:38.840 --> 03:40.100
<b>Blah, blah, yadda yadda...</b>

03:41.870 --> 03:44.870
<b>Takahiro Mizusawa: Conversation: S
Academics: A / Sports: A / Friendship: A / Effort: D</b>

03:42.290 --> 03:44.870
<b><i>And the third arrow, Mizusawa.</i></b>

03:44.870 --> 04:00.760
<b>Classroom / Konno's Motivation Meter / Day/Month</b>

03:45.450 --> 03:46.280
<b>Hey, Erika.</b>

03:46.860 --> 03:49.820
<b>Shuji says he's looking 
forward to the sports tournament.</b>

03:50.530 --> 03:52.930
<b>Yeah, he's one of those 
athletic guys, y'know?</b>

03:52.930 --> 03:55.630
<b>And girls who are good 
at sports? Totally his type.</b>

03:56.110 --> 03:59.510
<b><i>I think this one might actually be 
the most effective.</i></b>

04:00.400 --> 04:01.280
<b><i>I mean...</i></b>

04:01.010 --> 04:06.270
<b>Way Home / Konno's Motivation Meter / Day/Month</b>

04:01.280 --> 04:05.220
<b><i>Konno doesn't even know 
yet that Nakamura and Izumi are dating.</i></b>

04:06.610 --> 04:09.020
<b><i>Could be a little distracting, though...</i></b>

04:09.020 --> 04:11.020
<b>Girls' Softball</b>

04:17.410 --> 04:18.900
<b>I'm going for a home run!</b>

04:24.120 --> 04:26.120
<b>Girls' Softball</b>

04:31.190 --> 04:33.670
<b><i>"I want to make my friend Izumi happy."</i></b>

04:34.570 --> 04:36.880
<b><i>"I don't want Aoi Hinami 
to look down on me."</i></b>

04:37.730 --> 04:39.880
<b><i>"I want Nakamura to find me attractive."</i></b>

04:40.540 --> 04:43.220
<b><i>These three wants can 
all be satisfied by simply</i></b>

04:43.220 --> 04:44.960
<b><i>"doing my best in the sports tournament."</i></b>

04:45.540 --> 04:46.300
<b><i>In other words...</i></b>

04:49.500 --> 04:53.780
<b><i>Erika Konno reaped great 
rewards for little effort.</i></b>

04:55.630 --> 04:56.770
<b><i>Meanwhile,</i></b>

04:56.770 --> 04:58.390
<b><i>in the boys' basketball event,</i></b>

04:58.860 --> 05:00.900
<b><i>Nakamura and Mizusawa, along with</i></b>

05:00.900 --> 05:03.540
<b><i>Tachibana of the basketball club, 
moved onward to victory.</i></b>

05:05.330 --> 05:08.990
<b><i>In fact, Hinami had given me a task 
for the basketball game as well.</i></b>

05:09.080 --> 05:10.710
<b>Lay-Up Shots</b>

05:10.710 --> 05:13.210
<b>Lay-Up Shots</b>

05:11.090 --> 05:12.830
<b>Lay-up practice.</b>

05:13.460 --> 05:15.710
<b>Stay in a position 
where you can aim for a basket,</b>

05:15.710 --> 05:17.710
<b>and whenever you get 
the ball, make the shot.</b>

05:18.220 --> 05:20.340
<b>If you can contribute to a win with that,</b>

05:21.030 --> 05:23.840
<b>you'll gain an 
in with the athletic types, too,</b>

05:23.840 --> 05:25.490
<b>like Tachibana.</b>

05:26.310 --> 05:27.340
<b>I see...</b>

05:28.360 --> 05:32.860
<b><i>And so I spent the days 
before the tournament practicing my lay-ups.</i></b>

05:41.790 --> 05:44.260
<b><i>Hinami was kind enough to tag along...</i></b>

05:46.190 --> 05:49.320
<b><i>but now I'm watching the game 
from the bench.</i></b>

05:49.970 --> 05:54.830
<b><i>I ended up racking up 
a flurry of fouls first thing.</i></b>

05:56.640 --> 05:57.710
<b>You're outta here!</b>

06:00.340 --> 06:02.140
<b>That's Brain for you!</b>

06:06.940 --> 06:08.510
<b>And that's the game!</b>

06:08.850 --> 06:10.850
<b>Victory</b>

06:11.500 --> 06:12.650
<b>Shake it off, Fumiya.</b>

06:13.150 --> 06:14.060
<b>Can it, will you?</b>

06:14.060 --> 06:17.930
<b>Army Boy! Who gets ejected 
in the first thirty seconds?</b>

06:17.930 --> 06:19.810
<b>You really flopped it out there, Fumin.</b>

06:20.070 --> 06:22.440
<b>Man, that was amazing!</b>

06:22.440 --> 06:24.780
<b>Spare me, Tachibana...</b>

06:25.870 --> 06:27.660
<b><i>And in the end,</i></b>

06:27.650 --> 06:31.180
<b><i>both our teams came in first place,</i></b>

06:27.660 --> 06:33.910
<b>Congrats to This Year's Winners! / 2-2 / Boys' Basketball: 1st / Girls' Softball: 1st</b>

06:31.180 --> 06:33.580
<b><i>clinching our class's victory this year.</i></b>

06:34.180 --> 06:37.880
<b>We're number one!</b>

06:39.980 --> 06:41.540
<b><i>Fantastic!</i></b>

06:41.540 --> 06:43.160
<b>Victory hugs!</b>

06:42.500 --> 06:44.430
<b><i>Everyone's really enjoying themselves.</i></b>

06:44.930 --> 06:47.680
<b><i>It's like the entire class 
had come together as one.</i></b>

06:48.260 --> 06:51.090
<b><i>What a wonderful happy ending this was.</i></b>

06:54.540 --> 06:58.930
<b><i>But soon enough I would come to learn</i></b>

07:01.200 --> 07:04.690
<b><i>that this game of life 
isn't quite so simple.</i></b>

07:09.830 --> 07:13.250
<b><i>It started the day 
after the sports tournament.</i></b>

07:17.480 --> 07:18.280
<b>Oops.</b>

07:18.280 --> 07:19.410
<b>Sor-ry.</b>

07:20.000 --> 07:20.910
<b>It's fine.</b>

07:22.440 --> 07:26.420
<b><i>These little "accidents" kept on happening.</i></b>

07:27.360 --> 07:31.930
<b><i>A paper airplane would "accidentally" 
hit Hirabayashi during a break,</i></b>

07:37.390 --> 07:42.090
<b><i>or Konno would "accidentally" 
bump into her desk.</i></b>

07:43.820 --> 07:45.530
<b><i>Then, some days later,</i></b>

07:46.390 --> 07:49.260
<b><i>I realized, along with most of my classmates,</i></b>

07:50.190 --> 07:54.230
<b><i>that there was clear 
malicious intent behind it.</i></b>

07:57.540 --> 08:00.000
<b>I caused all this.</b>

08:00.250 --> 08:03.850
<b>Because it got out 
that you were dating Nakamura?</b>

08:04.270 --> 08:05.370
<b>Probably.</b>

08:05.370 --> 08:09.760
<b>Lashing out at me 
or Shuji would be too obvious.</b>

08:10.300 --> 08:12.530
<b>Instead, she went after Hirabayashi.</b>

08:14.170 --> 08:17.180
<b>I probably shouldn't say anything to Erika.</b>

08:18.240 --> 08:19.900
<b>Yeah, maybe so.</b>

08:23.140 --> 08:24.490
<b>I agree.</b>

08:25.380 --> 08:28.020
<b>Yuzu shouldn't say a word to Konno.</b>

08:28.300 --> 08:29.590
<b>You think so?</b>

08:30.160 --> 08:32.570
<b>This harassment is small potatoes.</b>

08:32.910 --> 08:35.300
<b>She can play it all off as purely 
accidental, and that'll be that.</b>

08:36.060 --> 08:38.330
<b>If we don't want the situation to get worse,</b>

08:38.330 --> 08:41.400
<b>the smartest course of action right 
now would be to watch silently.</b>

08:41.840 --> 08:42.540
<b>Hey...</b>

08:43.330 --> 08:45.640
<b>Is life <i>really</i> a god-tier game?</b>

08:46.530 --> 08:47.690
<b>What do you mean?</b>

08:48.340 --> 08:53.670
<b>I mean, we've got an irrational 
negative event with no reason behind it.</b>

08:54.480 --> 08:56.050
<b>There are reasons, all right.</b>

08:56.820 --> 08:59.640
<b>Erika Konno liked Nakamura.</b>

09:00.110 --> 09:04.740
<b>Thanks to our help, 
Yuzu started going out with Nakamura.</b>

09:05.560 --> 09:09.270
<b>Erika Konno kicked in, and our class won.</b>

09:10.020 --> 09:13.040
<b>Yuzu's relationship 
with Nakamura became public.</b>

09:13.830 --> 09:16.970
<b>Hirabayashi is a timid girl.</b>

09:17.790 --> 09:21.060
<b>All of those events just fell like dominoes.</b>

09:21.610 --> 09:25.290
<b>What's happening now isn't irrational--
it was practically inevitable.</b>

09:25.480 --> 09:27.170
<b>What do you mean, inevitable?</b>

09:27.480 --> 09:31.050
<b>Are you saying Hirabayashi 
has to just take her lumps?</b>

09:31.530 --> 09:32.800
<b>Well, yeah.</b>

09:33.080 --> 09:34.140
<b>Hinami...</b>

09:35.020 --> 09:39.430
<b>What's more, I don't personally see 
the need to help her at this juncture.</b>

09:40.920 --> 09:45.790
<b>I mean, this is the kind of 
harassment one can solve on one's own.</b>

09:46.140 --> 09:49.440
<b>Just because Hirabayashi 
doesn't intend to do so--</b>

09:49.870 --> 09:51.820
<b>C'mon, that's going too far!</b>

09:52.090 --> 09:55.390
<b>Look, we haven't seen anything that suggests</b>

09:55.390 --> 09:57.460
<b>Hirabayashi means to solve 
this problem on her own.</b>

09:58.190 --> 10:02.830
<b>Doesn't that make Hirabayashi herself 
another reason for Konno's behavior?</b>

10:03.130 --> 10:05.830
<b>So now Hirabayashi is responsible for it?</b>

10:06.040 --> 10:09.450
<b>Erika Konno's methods are cowardly 
and awful, absolutely.</b>

10:09.450 --> 10:10.840
<b>Konno is in the wrong.</b>

10:10.840 --> 10:12.420
<b>No two ways about that.</b>

10:13.150 --> 10:17.400
<b>But it's the gamer who's 
gripping the controller,</b>

10:17.400 --> 10:19.690
<b>clearing a path through 
the situation at hand.</b>

10:19.690 --> 10:21.350
<b>The same goes for life. Isn't that right?</b>

10:21.350 --> 10:23.940
<b>For you and me, maybe!</b>

10:23.940 --> 10:26.170
<b>But to require everyone to be a gamer...</b>

10:26.170 --> 10:28.780
<b>If someone tries to 
change something themselves</b>

10:28.780 --> 10:31.100
<b>and winds up not being able to 
solve the problem at hand,</b>

10:31.100 --> 10:33.560
<b>I will help--enthusiastically so.</b>

10:34.190 --> 10:38.530
<b>But if they don't even <i>try</i> 
to fix things on their own...</b>

10:39.230 --> 10:40.780
<b>I'm not required to help.</b>

10:41.290 --> 10:42.910
<b>That's not my thinking.</b>

10:43.350 --> 10:45.910
<b>I think it's the gamer who's in the right.</b>

10:46.500 --> 10:50.250
<b>And right now, 
Hirabayashi isn't trying to be a gamer.</b>

10:50.700 --> 10:53.540
<b>I mean, I <i>do</i> intend to do <i>something</i></b>

10:53.880 --> 10:55.650
<b>if things get any worse.</b>

10:56.570 --> 10:57.490
<b>I see...</b>

10:58.590 --> 11:04.050
<b>Hey, <i>you're</i> not considering doing 
something about this, are you?</b>

11:04.520 --> 11:07.060
<b>If there's something I <i>can</i> do, I'll do it.</b>

11:07.500 --> 11:08.280
<b>Aha.</b>

11:08.700 --> 11:13.020
<b>Well, proceed carefully, 
so things don't get worse.</b>

11:14.480 --> 11:16.620
<b>You can go without 
an assignment for a while.</b>

11:16.910 --> 11:17.960
<b>Got it.</b>

11:23.890 --> 11:25.020
<b>Like, what gives?</b>

11:25.020 --> 11:25.930
<b>I know, right?</b>

11:25.930 --> 11:26.740
<b>For real?</b>

11:26.740 --> 11:28.700
<b>That's what he said!</b>

11:28.910 --> 11:30.210
<b>Too funny!</b>

11:30.970 --> 11:32.240
<b>I was over the moon!</b>

11:32.980 --> 11:33.760
<b>Konno!</b>

11:35.680 --> 11:37.100
<b>How long are you going to do this?</b>

11:37.100 --> 11:39.990
<b>Enough nonsense! Cut it out already!</b>

11:40.970 --> 11:42.970
<b>Bottom-Tier Character Tomozaki S2</b>

11:43.660 --> 11:44.970
<b>How long are you going to do this?</b>

11:46.010 --> 11:48.850
<b>Enough nonsense! Cut it out already!</b>

11:49.180 --> 11:51.230
<b>Huh? What are you talking about?</b>

11:51.490 --> 11:53.110
<b>Don't give me that!</b>

11:53.110 --> 11:56.470
<b>Just because Nakamura's taken 
doesn't mean you can lash out at people!</b>

11:57.950 --> 11:58.990
<b>Huh...</b>

12:10.690 --> 12:11.810
<b>Ooh, Hanabi!</b>

12:11.810 --> 12:14.120
<b>You okay? You're shaking like a leaf.</b>

12:15.130 --> 12:16.000
<b>Shut up!</b>

12:16.690 --> 12:18.790
<b>Ow...</b>

12:20.060 --> 12:21.970
<b>I-I didn't hit you that hard--</b>

12:22.740 --> 12:24.800
<b>You started it.</b>

12:28.810 --> 12:30.240
<b>Uh-oh...</b>

12:42.220 --> 12:44.200
<b>Oops. Sor-ry.</b>

12:48.740 --> 12:52.100
<b><i>There it was, out in the open, 
almost too clear-cut:</i></b>

12:52.100 --> 12:53.890
<b><i>Erika Konno's maliciousness,</i></b>

12:54.810 --> 12:57.570
<b><i>now targeted at Tama.</i></b>

12:59.130 --> 13:01.590
<b>Konno! You did that on purpose!</b>

13:01.820 --> 13:04.590
<b>Huh? Lay off the assumptions, would you?</b>

13:04.590 --> 13:06.050
<b><i>What</i> assumptions?!</b>

13:06.310 --> 13:08.050
<b>Besides, I apologized, didn't I?</b>

13:08.050 --> 13:10.680
<b>You know that's not the issue here!</b>

13:10.910 --> 13:13.020
<b>What, you gonna hit me again?</b>

13:14.440 --> 13:16.650
<b>I'm against violence.</b>

13:17.350 --> 13:19.940
<b>Well, I'm not <i>using</i> violence!</b>

13:25.700 --> 13:27.340
<b>You're in the right here, Tama.</b>

13:28.150 --> 13:29.950
<b>You okay, Tama?</b>

13:30.170 --> 13:31.310
<b>I'm fine.</b>

13:31.310 --> 13:32.150
<b>Hanabi...</b>

13:33.160 --> 13:34.240
<b>It's okay.</b>

13:35.310 --> 13:36.980
<b>I'll... I'll do something.</b>

13:38.530 --> 13:39.510
<b>Aoi?</b>

13:41.430 --> 13:44.500
<b><i>Konno's attacks continued.</i></b>

13:45.000 --> 13:48.220
<b><i>She would "accidentally" bump 
into Tama's desk,</i></b>

13:48.580 --> 13:52.980
<b><i>or one of her cronies would 
"accidentally" knock Tama's chair over;</i></b>

13:53.980 --> 13:57.890
<b><i>all of Tama's pencil leads would 
"accidentally" wind up broken,</i></b>

13:58.940 --> 14:03.280
<b><i>or the Konno girls would "accidentally" 
trash-talk her loud enough in conversation</i></b>

14:03.280 --> 14:05.110
<b><i>that Tama could hear it loud and clear.</i></b>

14:06.090 --> 14:08.710
<b><i>But unlike when it happened 
to Hirabayashi...</i></b>

14:09.280 --> 14:11.520
<b>Konno! I <i>know</i> you kicked my desk again!</b>

14:12.090 --> 14:16.350
<b><i>...every time Konno hurt Tama, 
Tama called her out.</i></b>

14:16.850 --> 14:19.710
<b>Geez, will you stop 
with the false accusations already?</b>

14:19.710 --> 14:21.090
<b>You did it yesterday, too!</b>

14:21.340 --> 14:25.840
<b>Did you forget that time 
you used violence against me?</b>

14:26.780 --> 14:28.340
<b>That was an accident!</b>

14:28.340 --> 14:31.600
<b>Huh? No, what <i>I</i> did was an accident.</b>

14:31.600 --> 14:34.010
<b>What <i>you</i> did?</b>

14:34.450 --> 14:36.600
<b>All. On. Purpose.</b>

14:38.780 --> 14:41.040
<b>Stop, Tama! Whoa, girl!</b>

14:41.040 --> 14:43.670
<b>Okay, Hanabi--time to cool off.</b>

14:45.670 --> 14:50.070
<b><i>Hinami and Mimimi would calm her down 
so she wouldn't get even more furious.</i></b>

14:50.550 --> 14:53.830
<b><i>This pattern repeated itself 
over several days.</i></b>

14:54.110 --> 14:56.540
<b>Hanabi really has it rough...</b>

14:56.890 --> 14:58.390
<b>She sure does.</b>

14:58.390 --> 15:00.720
<b>First Hirabayashi, now Hanabi--</b>

15:00.720 --> 15:03.000
<b>it's like she doesn't care <i>who</i> she torments.</b>

15:03.000 --> 15:04.160
<b>Right?</b>

15:04.160 --> 15:06.340
<b>That Natsubayashi 
is really something else...</b>

15:06.620 --> 15:10.340
<b>I never expected her to keep pushing 
back on Konno like that, did you?</b>

15:10.780 --> 15:13.040
<b>She's way gutsier 
than she looks, that's for sure.</b>

15:13.690 --> 15:14.740
<b>Still...</b>

15:14.740 --> 15:18.290
<b>Konno may be terrible, 
but Natsubayashi gets way too angry.</b>

15:19.040 --> 15:22.050
<b>Not that Natsubayashi is in the wrong here!</b>

15:22.500 --> 15:25.480
<b>Hmm... I wish they'd 
handle it a little better.</b>

15:25.950 --> 15:28.940
<b>No one wants to see that every dang day.</b>

15:29.630 --> 15:31.470
<b>How many times is it, anyway?</b>

15:31.470 --> 15:34.870
<b>Why even is Natsubayashi 
still getting so mad?</b>

15:35.160 --> 15:37.250
<b>I get that Konno is terrible, 
but doesn't she understand</b>

15:37.250 --> 15:41.170
<b>that all this classroom bickering 
just sours the whole mood?</b>

15:41.500 --> 15:45.500
<b>Well, Natsubayashi never did know 
how to read a room.</b>

15:46.590 --> 15:50.010
<b><i>Eventually, the class's 
mood went all off-kilter.</i></b>

15:50.410 --> 15:52.760
<b><i>Hinami was the one who put a stop to it.</i></b>

15:53.390 --> 15:58.170
<b><i>She stirred up sympathy for Tama, 
aimed at the middle-ranking girls.</i></b>

15:58.680 --> 16:01.520
<b><i>Mimimi tried to be 
with Tama as much as possible</i></b>

16:01.520 --> 16:03.320
<b><i>whenever we were on break.</i></b>

16:04.180 --> 16:07.500
<b><i>She'd hustle Tama out of the classroom, 
avoiding contact with Konno.</i></b>

16:08.380 --> 16:10.310
<b><i>The efforts of these two</i></b>

16:10.650 --> 16:14.730
<b><i>kept something truly momentous 
from taking place.</i></b>

16:15.910 --> 16:17.910
<b>Sewing Room 2</b>

16:17.040 --> 16:17.910
<b>This Tama thing--</b>

16:18.280 --> 16:20.050
<b>it really went sour, eh?</b>

16:20.650 --> 16:21.540
<b>Yeah...</b>

16:22.140 --> 16:24.630
<b>You and Mimimi have her back for now,</b>

16:25.060 --> 16:28.050
<b>but at this rate, she'll only 
become more and more isolated.</b>

16:28.780 --> 16:31.090
<b>Right. It can't go on like this.</b>

16:31.440 --> 16:32.630
<b>We have to do something.</b>

16:33.360 --> 16:37.680
<b><i>Lately it felt like Hinami hadn't been 
going about things in her usual way.</i></b>

16:38.120 --> 16:39.870
<b><i>It's not that her methods were </i>wrong<i>;</i></b>

16:40.350 --> 16:43.600
<b><i>she just wasn't the same old Hinami.</i></b>

16:44.390 --> 16:45.810
<b>Hey, Hinami...</b>

16:46.210 --> 16:46.890
<b>What?</b>

16:47.540 --> 16:52.030
<b>I think helping Tama is 
the most important thing right now.</b>

16:52.030 --> 16:53.570
<b>More than anything else.</b>

16:54.290 --> 16:55.780
<b>And?</b>

16:56.360 --> 17:00.710
<b>And we could maybe ask her, you know,</b>

17:00.710 --> 17:03.960
<b>to stop striking back at Konno, or...</b>

17:03.960 --> 17:05.330
<b>Absolutely not.</b>

17:06.380 --> 17:07.920
<b>Hanabi is right.</b>

17:08.300 --> 17:09.950
<b>The situation is what's wrong.</b>

17:10.610 --> 17:12.760
<b>Hanabi does <i>not</i> need to change.</b>

17:14.720 --> 17:17.970
<b>Good Suggestion / Bad Rule</b>

17:15.260 --> 17:19.600
<b><i>This was the exact opposite of what 
Hinami had been insisting thus far.</i></b>

17:20.570 --> 17:25.230
<b><i>If the situation is wrong, 
we should fight in a way that fits it--</i></b>

17:25.870 --> 17:28.730
<b><i>even if it means outwardly 
distorting ourselves.</i></b>

17:30.830 --> 17:35.450
<b><i>That's her policy, the way she 
racked up all those wins--or it </i>was<i>.</i></b>

17:38.990 --> 17:43.870
<b><i>After class, Mimimi asked me to join 
her and Tama on the way home.</i></b>

17:44.230 --> 17:47.370
<b><i>Hinami stayed late for student council work.</i></b>

17:47.720 --> 17:49.880
<b>Oh! You've got some 
whipped cream on you, Tama!</b>

17:49.880 --> 17:51.350
<b>Huh? Really?</b>

17:53.020 --> 17:54.330
<b>Don't mind if I do!</b>

17:54.800 --> 17:56.520
<b>Hey! Why'd you eat it?</b>

17:56.520 --> 17:58.550
<b>Mmm, delicious!</b>

17:58.550 --> 18:00.640
<b>She doesn't like that, Mimimi.</b>

18:00.640 --> 18:03.090
<b>What? Sure you do, right?</b>

18:03.090 --> 18:05.640
<b>Of course I don't! Isn't it obvious?</b>

18:05.640 --> 18:07.870
<b>Ack! What a shock!</b>

18:16.900 --> 18:19.970
<b>How did things get to this point?</b>

18:20.700 --> 18:23.770
<b>Bad luck, bad timing...</b>

18:23.770 --> 18:26.550
<b>Tama hasn't even done anything wrong.</b>

18:26.550 --> 18:28.790
<b>Everyone's making her out 
to be the bad guy...</b>

18:29.210 --> 18:31.580
<b>I hate watching that happen!</b>

18:35.430 --> 18:37.050
<b>Hey, Tomozaki.</b>

18:38.040 --> 18:40.290
<b>Am I doing a good job?</b>

18:41.060 --> 18:43.060
<b>You know: cheering her up?</b>

18:43.950 --> 18:44.840
<b>Yeah.</b>

18:45.760 --> 18:47.750
<b>I think you are.</b>

18:49.190 --> 18:51.190
<b>Tomozaki</b>

18:51.470 --> 18:55.190
<b><i>At this point, Mimimi's goal must be</i></b>

18:57.200 --> 19:00.650
<b><i>for Erika Konno to give 
in to Tama's resistance.</i></b>

18:57.820 --> 18:58.450
<b>Hanabi Natsubayashi resists!</b>

18:58.450 --> 18:58.830
<b>Erika Konno take 0 damage</b>

18:58.830 --> 18:59.410
<b>Erika Konno: I'm against violence!</b>

18:59.410 --> 19:00.410
<b>Hanabi Natsubayashi takes 170 damage!!</b>

19:01.950 --> 19:02.950
<b>Minami Nanami: Tama~~!!</b>

19:02.950 --> 19:03.830
<b>Minami Nanami: Mimimi's here ♪</b>

19:03.470 --> 19:06.600
<b><i>If Konno's harassment stops</i></b>

19:03.830 --> 19:05.210
<b>Minami Nanami: You okay, Tama?!</b>

19:05.210 --> 19:06.960
<b>Minami Nanami: All patched up ♪</b>

19:06.600 --> 19:08.600
<b><i>while Mimimi is looking after Tama,</i></b>

19:07.960 --> 19:08.960
<b>Erika Konno: (...Not funny)</b>

19:08.960 --> 19:09.960
<b>Erika Konno: (Forget this...)</b>

19:09.960 --> 19:13.210
<b>Erika Konno left...</b>

19:11.250 --> 19:13.210
<b><i>we'd get the good ending.</i></b>

19:15.010 --> 19:18.750
<b><i>Hinami was controlling the mood 
of the class as a whole,</i></b>

19:15.470 --> 19:15.970
<b>Erika Konno manipulates the mood</b>

19:15.970 --> 19:16.470
<b>The good/bad norm!</b>

19:16.470 --> 19:16.970
<b>Hanabi Natsubayashi takes 170 damage!!</b>

19:16.970 --> 19:17.470
<b>Aoi Hinami: Hanabi...</b>

19:17.470 --> 19:18.970
<b>Aoi Hinami: I'll figure it out...</b>

19:18.750 --> 19:20.170
<b><i>buying more time.</i></b>

19:18.970 --> 19:20.970
<b>Aoi Hinami manipulates the mood</b>

19:20.920 --> 19:22.670
<b><i>If all goes well,</i></b>

19:20.970 --> 19:21.970
<b>The good/bad norm reverses!</b>

19:21.970 --> 19:23.220
<b>Classmate x6 take 300 damage!!</b>

19:23.140 --> 19:27.190
<b>the mood--the norm for good 
or bad-- will be flipped on its head,</b>

19:23.220 --> 19:24.230
<b>Erika Konno takes 100 damage!!</b>

19:25.100 --> 19:27.980
<b>Classmate x6 joined the party!!</b>

19:27.190 --> 19:30.550
<b><i>and she'll start painting 
Konno as one of the bad ones.</i></b>

19:28.980 --> 19:30.230
<b>Erika Konno: (...Not funny)</b>

19:30.230 --> 19:31.400
<b>Erika Konno: (Forget this...)</b>

19:31.400 --> 19:33.230
<b>Erika Konno left...</b>

19:32.370 --> 19:35.130
<b><i>But I have a different strategy in mind.</i></b>

19:33.990 --> 19:35.480
<b>Fumiya Tomozaki / Hanabi Natsubayashi / Erika Konno</b>

19:35.490 --> 19:40.990
<b>Erika Konno glares steadily</b>

19:35.870 --> 19:37.540
<b><i>What we need to aim for now</i></b>

19:37.540 --> 19:41.160
<b><i>is getting past all this 
without hurting Tama.</i></b>

19:41.650 --> 19:45.160
<b><i>And for that, we can use a tactic 
that every gamer knows:</i></b>

19:41.740 --> 19:46.750
<b>Fumiya Tomozaki: (Thinking...)</b>

19:45.810 --> 19:47.710
<b><i>Retreat.</i></b>

19:46.750 --> 19:47.750
<b>Fumiya Tomozaki: Tama! We're running!</b>

19:47.750 --> 19:49.630
<b>Tama: !!</b>

19:48.190 --> 19:51.250
<b><i>The option to take time off school 
until everything blows over.</i></b>

19:49.630 --> 19:51.250
<b>Successfully escaped</b>

19:52.040 --> 19:53.890
<b><i>Sure, it's a little backward.</i></b>

19:54.450 --> 19:58.760
<b><i>But it WILL get us to the goal, 
as "wrong" or dirty as it may be.</i></b>

19:59.330 --> 20:02.470
<b><i>NO NAME can't do that, but I can.</i></b>

20:02.780 --> 20:04.570
<b><i>That's the nanashi way.</i></b>

20:07.890 --> 20:10.020
<b>Old AV Room</b>

20:10.140 --> 20:12.180
<b>What did you want?</b>

20:12.550 --> 20:13.770
<b>Well, um...</b>

20:14.020 --> 20:17.520
<b>This thing with Erika Konno and everybody...</b>

20:19.300 --> 20:22.050
<b>You know, Aoi once told me...</b>

20:22.050 --> 20:24.990
<b>She said you're a little bit like me.</b>

20:25.500 --> 20:28.130
<b>You just come out 
and say what you're thinking.</b>

20:28.130 --> 20:30.000
<b>Yeah... maybe I do.</b>

20:30.320 --> 20:33.190
<b>So what's this about Konno and everybody?</b>

20:33.430 --> 20:34.250
<b>Right.</b>

20:34.910 --> 20:40.560
<b>It must be hard with Konno attacking you 
and everyone else avoiding you.</b>

20:41.020 --> 20:45.140
<b>And if it is, I wonder 
if it might be better to remove yourself.</b>

20:48.890 --> 20:50.140
<b>It <i>is</i> hard.</b>

20:51.580 --> 20:52.530
<b>But you know...</b>

20:53.650 --> 20:55.320
<b>I'm fine.</b>

20:56.350 --> 21:00.400
<b>When I remind myself 
that I'm in the right, I'm fine.</b>

21:01.410 --> 21:05.700
<b>Breaking the Hanabi 
that believes in things would be worse.</b>

21:07.020 --> 21:09.780
<b>Okay. Then you'll be all right.</b>

21:10.400 --> 21:14.080
<b>I've been playing games 
on my own all this time.</b>

21:14.240 --> 21:16.460
<b>And all this time, I've been thinking:</b>

21:16.940 --> 21:20.770
<b>The righteousness inside me is more important 
than how people see me.</b>

21:21.990 --> 21:25.340
<b>Uh-huh. As long as I can be myself,</b>

21:25.340 --> 21:27.030
<b>I can put up with anything.</b>

21:28.310 --> 21:29.810
<b>But you know, Tomozaki...</b>

21:30.760 --> 21:32.830
<b>Minmi's so sad.</b>

21:34.160 --> 21:36.880
<b>And that's why I want to change.</b>

21:38.350 --> 21:41.380
<b>I guess I really <i>am</i> like you.</b>

21:41.810 --> 21:45.650
<b>I just say what I think, 
and I suck at bending myself to fit.</b>

21:46.000 --> 21:48.940
<b>Actually, I think you've 
changed a lot lately.</b>

21:48.940 --> 21:52.150
<b>You're better at reading a room, 
better at fitting in.</b>

21:52.150 --> 21:56.340
<b>You're like me, but you're challenging 
yourself with your weaknesses.</b>

21:56.340 --> 21:58.960
<b>I didn't think that was possible.</b>

22:01.190 --> 22:03.420
<b>So show me how you do it.</b>

22:06.420 --> 22:09.510
<b>Teach me how to fight, too.</b>
